  "_about": "Skill ids here are Skua skillIds 0-4: id N = in-game key N+1 (id 0 = auto attack = key 1, id 4 = the 5th key). Guides count keys (vault KNOWLEDGE/Combat-Mechanics section 0); comments below say \"id\" or \"key\" explicitly. Seraph merges these over Skua's AdvancedSkills.json into each engine's UserAdvancedSkills.json. Rotations first measured live on the Class Hall dummy with the Battle Analyzer (2026-09-23, KB Key Spammer tests). HP/aura conditions kept so the bots stay safe. 2026-10-16 (the owner): every boss class has a normal mode (Base/Atk, easy bosses) and a careful mode Solo (hard bosses) that the class ladder (lib/fightplan.js) switches to through CBO SoloModeSelect. 2026-10-19 (the owner, main got LR + Arcana Invoker): LR Solo = careful: Wicked Purgatory (id 2 = key 3, up to 40% less damage taken at 5 Enveloped stacks) and Depraved Empowerment (id 3 = key 4, Arcane Shield + party HoT) before damage, Atramentous Shade (id 1 = key 2, the Decay) only above 40% mana (aqwwiki legion-revenant-class). 2026-10-19 Arcana Invoker measured on the dummy (combat packets, 8 min runs, vault JOURNAL/2026-10-19): id 1 (The Beginning and the End) only with no cycle (no Fool, no World) or on Judgement - pressed inside The World it ends The World and restarts at The Fool (13k DPS against 24-30k), so The World is never left early: its damage ramps the longer it lasts. Base = that (also Nightbane: true damage ignores resistance). Solo = careful: also id 1 inside The World below 35% HP (back to The Fool's +80% damage resistance; End of the World stacks cost 4% each). No skipOnMatch: a skipped rule makes Skua cast the NEXT skill unchecked (ScriptSkill.cs), which could fire an ungated id 1. Revocation (id 3) needs 40 mana. 2026-10-20 (community research, vault STRATEGY/Research-2026-10-20): King's Echo CORVAK (id 4) on 8 Residual Energy / 6 + mana < 40% / mana < 20% (was: mana <= 60%, before the stacks were built), King's Shield (id 3) still straight after it (the owner 2026-10-16); Chrono ShadowHunter/ShadowSlayer rift rotation (ids 3x6, 4, 1) for Base and Solo; Void Highlord Solo checked: already the stay-Shackled hard-hitter line.",
